 "notes": "The Heart (boss_heart). Built on templates\\heart_template.flp (vael_template with its parts' names; channel 'bells' = Analog Harp on insert 2, replacing the organ; 'bell_clock' = the unused Clock Bell): strings_full on Staccato Blend (insert 5, advance 0.06; keys 50/62/64 read -11..-20 c on the fundamental but +0..+11 c on h2-h8, so no clone pitch fixes both: left as is), choir on Ah Voice (4), brass on Trumpfal (6), timpani on Gong & Timpani (+1, insert 7), all seven bells on the Analog Harp (they enter one after another in bars 19-34 and share a stem). v1 had the bells on the Clock Bell, which scatters 15-25 c above D5. v2 (review v1 MAJOR): the bells channel's Analog Harp is struck, not held (both VCA rows decay 1.46 s, sustain 0, release ~0.41 s; projects\\boss_heart_v2raw.flp), so the seven motifs stay apart; brass -3 dB at 2.5 kHz and high cut 5.5 kHz (it was 63-65 % of the 2-6 kHz energy). Struck bells measure ~10 dB under the held ones over their active time; their target is -31.5 (a struck onset reads louder than its average)."
